      "detailed_figure_description": "Hand-drawn simple circuit. A battery on the left is labeled V, with a pink plus sign at its upper terminal and a blue minus sign at its lower terminal. A black wire forms a rectangular loop. Blue arrows labeled I show conventional current moving clockwise: rightward across the top, downward along the right side, and leftward across the bottom. Black arrows and repeated e⁻ labels show electrons moving in the opposite, counterclockwise direction around the loop and downward through the battery.",
