      "page": 1,
      "source_regions": [
        "page-1-r0003"
      ],
      "text": "Electrical current (I) is the rate of flow of positive charge.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "id": "page-1-s0004",
      "normalized_math": "I = \\frac{Q}{\\Delta t} = \\frac{Q}{t}",
      "page": 1,
      "source_regions": [
        "page-1-r0004"
      ],
      "spoken_math_alternative": "I equals Q divided by delta t, which equals Q divided by t.",
      "type": "formula"
    },
    {
      "id": "page-1-s0005",
      "page": 1,
      "source_regions": [
        "page-1-r0005"
      ],
      "text": "It’s direction (from DC, or direct current, voltage) is opposite the ‘flow’ of electrons: from + to −.",
      "type": "paragraph"
